<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57041" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κέως</span></b> , ἡ,
		<u>Ceos</u>, one of the Cyclades, <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			12(5).532.7
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			10.5.6
		</span></i>, etc.:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κεῖος</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κήϊος</span></b> , ὁ, a <u>Ceian</u>, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			5.102
		</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ Χῖος, ἀλλὰ
		Κεῖος</span> not a (roguish) Chian, but an (honest)
		<u>Ceian</u>, proverb in <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Ra.</u>
			970
		</span></i>; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκόλαστόν τινα . . , καὶ οὐδαμῶς
					Κεῖον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					341e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				638b
			</span></i>; prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν Κέῳ τίς
			ἡμέρα</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Crates Com.
				29.5
			</span></i>. (Not to be confused with <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κέος</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				42(1).122.117
			</span></i>, or with <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κέος</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.76
			</span></i> (cf. <i>Wiener Sitzb.</i><i><span class="en">
				211(1).30
			</span></i>).)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
